      "mergeID": "6164853453961e23a7d546ec",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Please restore the \"icon indicating the Supported Platform\" for avatars on the \"Clone Public Avatar\" that was removed in the Open Beta.\nDue to the QM change in Open Beta, the blue and green (or gray) icons, indicating the Supported Platform for avatars used by others, that used to be on the \"Clone Public Avatar\" button (changes to \"Clone Not Allowed\" or \"Can't Clone Private\" depending on the situation) until [1134] have been removed.\nThis icon is one of what I have been relying on very heavily to play cross-platform VRChat.\nIn the Open Beta, the disappearance of the icon has caused the following problems.\n・Can’t recognize my own avatar\nWhen a PC user clones a public avatar, the user cannot determine whether a Quest users will see the same appearance or the fallback avatar until pointed it out by the Quest users. The same problem occurs when a Quest user clone a PC-unsupported avatar.\n・Occurrence of communication discrepancies\nWhen PC users and Quest users chat about the avatar they are wearing, it is likely to happen communication discrepancies. Especially in the case of chatting between beginners, cross-platform and fallback systems are often not understood. Many people are confused by the outward differences between them. Senior users have been checking and explaining the supported platforms of avatars, but the removing of the icon makes it difficult to do so.\n・Making cross-platform event management more difficult\nAlthough each player has a different attitude toward the above communication discrepancy, there are many events that do not take kindly to this and encourage players to participate with cross-platform avatars. This is especially emphasized at events where appearance is important such as role-playing events and gaming events. To run these events, it is important for the administrators to know the platform support status of the participants' avatars. But this is no longer possible.\nThese problems can be solved by restoring the blue and green icons on the \"Clone Public Avatar\" button to indicate the supported platform of the avatar, as in [1134]. However, there may be more efficient and better places to place the design. \nFor example, instead of \"Clone Public Avatar\", it could be displayed on the \"Show Avatar Stats\" button, which would allow users to check the status and supported platform of their own avatar as well as those of others in the new QM. I think this would be a more versatile improvement.\nIn addition, I think that displaying the icon on the nameplate that indicates the supported platform of the avatar (as well as the avatar's performance rank) will help reduce the risk of communication discrepancies.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1137] Can't check the supported platforms (PC/Quest) of other players’ avatars",
